{"assets":["/statement-assets/235df16a54fe1edd0b2cbc02f156fcfb2649ce6f08616bc62083fdd34d0f68e3.png","/statement-assets/abcaf51a57aca5bdfec427b8bb1436d61d187a8aff0f3f3285595282f4d975f5.png","/statement-assets/b061e73333bc83db4e043c9a8c60d02044ae1a100e98ada1a4b55bc004c403db.png","/statement-assets/82d6efd504ac5a77af915ded01a9c48108af6d6e12beca0f326ce4293e6634f4.png","/statement-assets/221a744e8c00dd7e366917eed4c6f65c945a134e29cf297d3ee20b37483c4505.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1666","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Admissible Map"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"map"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a matrix consisting of symbols from the set of '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"map graph"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a map matrix $$$a$$$ is a directed graph with $$$n \\cdot m$$$ vertices numbered as $$$(i, j)$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n; 1 \\le j \\le m$$$), where $$$n$$$ is the number of rows in the matrix, $$$m$$$ is the number of columns in the matrix. The graph has $$$n \\cdot m$$$ directed edges $$$(i, j) \\to (i + di_{a_{i, j}}, j + dj_{a_{i, j}})$$$, where $$$(di_U, dj_U) = (-1, 0)$$$; $$$(di_L, dj_L) = (0, -1)$$$; $$$(di_D, dj_D) = (1, 0)$$$; $$$(di_R, dj_R) = (0, 1)$$$. A map graph is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"valid"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" when all edges point to valid vertices in the graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"admissible map"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a map such that its map graph is valid and consists of a set of cycles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"description"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a map $$$a$$$ is a concatenation of all rows of the map — a string $$$a_{1,1} a_{1,2} \\ldots a_{1, m} a_{2, 1} \\ldots a_{n, m}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a string $$$s$$$. Your task is to find how many substrings of this string can constitute a description of some admissible map. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"substring"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a string $$$s_1s_2 \\ldots s_l$$$ of length $$$l$$$ is defined by a pair of indices $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ ($$$1 \\le p \\le q \\le l$$$) and is equal to $$$s_ps_{p+1} \\ldots s_q$$$. Two substrings of $$$s$$$ are considered different when the pair of their indices $$$(p, q)$$$ differs, even if they represent the same resulting string."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the only input line, there is a string $$$s$$$, consisting of at least one and at most $$$20\\,000$$$ symbols '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"U"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output one integer — the number of substrings of $$$s$$$ that constitute a description of some admissible map."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nRDUL\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nRDRU\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nRLRLRL\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there are two substrings that can constitute a description of an admissible map — \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RDUL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" as a matrix of size $$$2 \\times 2$$$ (pic. 1) and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"DU"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" as a matrix of size $$$2 \\times 1$$$ (pic. 2). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, no substring can constitute a description of an admissible map. E. g. if we try to look at the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RDRU"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" as a matrix of size $$$2 \\times 2$$$, we can find out that the resulting graph is not a set of cycles (pic. 3)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, three substrings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", two substrings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RLRL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and one substring \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RLRLRL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" can constitute an admissible map, some of them in multiple ways. E. g. here are two illustrations of substring \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RLRLRL"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" as matrices of size $$$3 \\times 2$$$ (pic. 4) and $$$1 \\times 6$$$ (pic. 5)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/235df16a54fe1edd0b2cbc02f156fcfb2649ce6f08616bc62083fdd34d0f68e3.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/abcaf51a57aca5bdfec427b8bb1436d61d187a8aff0f3f3285595282f4d975f5.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b061e73333bc83db4e043c9a8c60d02044ae1a100e98ada1a4b55bc004c403db.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/82d6efd504ac5a77af915ded01a9c48108af6d6e12beca0f326ce4293e6634f4.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/221a744e8c00dd7e366917eed4c6f65c945a134e29cf297d3ee20b37483c4505.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1666A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1666/problem/A"}